---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Settings" description="What your creative team can and cannot do." page="settings">
  <section class="paper" data-agent-summary="Settings: what the creative team can and cannot do.">
    <h2>How your team works</h2>
    <ul class="plain-list">
      <li><strong>Brand strategist</strong> interviews you one question at a time and proposes your answers, in your words, for the brand document.</li>
      <li><strong>Content strategist</strong> notes what makes your best posts, or the people who shaped you, unique, and proposes content map branches through your lens.</li>
      <li><strong>Writer</strong> drafts posts, threads, articles, newsletters and scripts from the map, in your voice.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="paper">
    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <ul class="plain-list">
      <li>Nothing the team proposes is saved until you approve it in the sidebar.</li>
      <li>It never posts, schedules or sends anything for you.</li>
      <li>It does not scrape social platforms and has no view counts. Paste your best posts on the Content page; research notes say what each idea is based on.</li>
      <li>Your brand interview, and the people, audiences and goals it names, go to your Wiki only as a change batch you review there. Everything else lives in this app's own database; export it with your other Outfitter data.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Layout>
<script>import "../scripts/editor";</script>
